  message: "Fixed in PR #2354 (dev 39bef1108). Kotlin and Python label each scope with the enclosing callable's name plus its hashed signature (Kotlin: also property, setter, init, enum entry). Extended under the general-fix rule to Scala, Dart, PHP, JS/TS, C++ and HLSL.\nFILED REPROS RE-RUN on dev 39bef1108 (the item's own files A.kt and a.py, analyzer output before the occurrence split, closure/presplit.py): Kotlin 3 tie groups to 0 (K.open in two constructors, K.helper in two overloads of f, K.g in two getters); Python 2 to 0 (g in a property getter and its setter, helper in two redefinitions of f). On dev 05ed6f5fe: 3 and 2.\nMEASURED by the builders: okhttp 709 of 11,117 ids moved, tie groups 38 to 0; poetry 122 of 4,125 moved, tie groups 3 to 3 (the three are not locals: @overload stubs over 60 characters).\nNOT FIXED, filed: WI-vijov-roham-momig-jovid-garat-hahov-bajih-tisat (locals of two unnamed holders, Python try/except twins), WI-zopan-fuviv-tuvam-foboz-rokof-jonod-kopus-julol (Kotlin and Scala companions); notes added on WI-gikif (long @overload stubs), WI-lusof (C# local functions are not emitted) and WI-dokos (JS/TS). JS/TS locals inside two anonymous callbacks still tie: noted on WI-dokos.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/closure/ (out_dev.txt = dev 39bef1108 after the merge, out_base.txt = dev 05ed6f5fe before it; repro trees t/, run.sh, q.py, presplit.py)."  # 2b1c
